To request a replacement Social Security card, you typically do not need to write a custom letter. The Social Security Administration (SSA) has a standardized process for this. 

Here is the best way to handle your request:

**1. Apply Online (Easiest Method)**
In most states, you can request a replacement card online for free by creating or logging into your personal **"my Social Security"** account on the official SSA website (ssa.gov). 

**2. Apply via Form SS-5**
If you cannot apply online, you will need to fill out **Form SS-5** (Application for a Social Security Card). You can download this form from the SSA website. Once completed, you can mail it or take it to your local Social Security office along with original unexpired documents proving your identity (like a U.S. driver's license, state-issued non-driver identification card, or U.S. passport).

**If you still need to provide a formal written request (e.g., as a cover letter for your mailed application), you can use this phrasing:**

> **Subject:** Request for Replacement Social Security Card
> 
> To Whom It May Concern at the Social Security Administration,
> 
> I am writing to formally request a replacement copy of my Social Security card. Enclosed with this letter, please find my completed Form SS-5 along with the required original documents to verify my identity and citizenship status. 
> 
> Please process this request and mail the replacement card to my address listed on the application form. If you need any additional information, please contact me at [Your Phone Number] or [Your Email Address].
> 
> Thank you for your time and assistance.
> 
> Sincerely,
> [Your Full Name]
> [Your Address]

*Security Note: Please be very careful about sharing your Social Security Number (SSN) online or with AI assistants. It is highly recommended to only provide your SSN directly through official, secure government portals or encrypted forms.*

